 11 | let noisy = process.run(process.request("/bin/sh", ["-c", "echo boom >&2; exit 3"]))?
    |                                         ^^^^^^^^^
    = cause: `process.request` or `process.spawn` receives a program whose basename ∈ {`sh bash dash zsh csh scripts ksh tcsh env xargs busybox python python3 perl ruby node`}; the basename is a literal string, or the literal tail of an interpolated string after its last `/`
    = suggestion: call the program you meant directly, with its arguments: `process.run(process.request(program, […]))`
